      "status": "mathematical proof reconstructed",
      "correspondence": "For a returning γ each column γ⁻¹e_j has q_(h₀) at most A B_j. Each finite ellipsoid bounds the choices for that one column. The ordered columns recover γ⁻¹, so the product bounds possible matrices. The written proof uses a union of these same finite sets and injectivity of the ordered columns.",
