    {
      "id": "OVL-02",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "title": "A locally finite orbit sum normalizes a smooth weight on the orbits meeting K",
      "anchor": "inputs-overlap-normalize",
      "statement": "For every number field and rank and each compact K in the positive cone, there exist a globally smooth nonnegative ψ and compact K′ inside the cone containing its support. Every orbit meeting K has ∑_γ ψ(γ⁻¹·h)=1. On each compact subset of the positive cone the sum uses a uniformly finite list.",
      "hypotheses": "N≥0. Nonnegative δ and every Hermitian k with Cl(δ,h,k) are allowed in the separate relative bound for ψ. The positive h need only meet K up to arithmetic translation for normalization.",
      "definitions": [
        "There is an ε>0 with compact closed thickening K′ inside the cone. A smooth f∈[0,1] has the open thickening as its nonzero set.",
        "b=f/m≥1 on K for its positive minimum m there; in the empty case b=0 and m=1.",
        "τ_γ h=γ⁻¹·h, τ_δτ_γ=τ_(γδ). The invariant S is the orbit sum of b and g(s)=1/2+(s−1/2)Θ(2s−1)."
      ],
