      "status": "mathematical proof reconstructed",
      "correspondence": "Properness on B∪K′ bounds the labels which can contribute anywhere on B. Apply this to small closed balls to get smoothness of S on the cone. The denominator g(S) is at least 1/2. It equals S wherever an orbit meets K. Compact support strictly inside the cone gives a smooth zero extension to all Hermitian tuples. The sum runs over group elements with stabilizer multiplicities.",
      "review": "An independent check reproduced the Eisenstein example: τ_γ I=γ*γ, U has 2·6²=72 elements, τ_γ I=s*s iff γ∈Us, and the two stabilizer packets give 72 weights of 1/216 and 72 of 1/108."
