    {
      "id": "OVL-03",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "title": "Equivariant pullback gives finite relative overlaps and the bump factor in the derivative bound",
      "anchor": "inputs-overlap-pullback",
      "statement": "For the positive-rank totally complex construction, φ=ψ∘F gives a locally finite partition on the entire positive cone. All relative return labels for its closed support belong up to inversion to Γ(K′). The bump has a relative Lipschitz witness Cψ=16/m+4LR, used before differentiation.",
      "hypotheses": "The corrected, normalized map F is smooth and equivariant on the cone, and all its values meet K up to translation by the two lower bounds on the minima. The constant L is an ordinary Lipschitz constant for ψ, and R≥0 bounds the matrix-entry norm on K′.",
      "definitions": [
        "The closure D of {φ≠0} is taken relative to the positive cone. It satisfies F(D)⊆K′.",
        "Cl(δ,h,k) means |q_k(z)−q_h(z)|≤δ q_h(z) for all archimedean z. The base h is positive.",
        "For labels γ,η meeting over h, η⁻¹γ moves F(γ⁻¹·h) to F(η⁻¹·h)."
      ],
