      "correspondence": "Apply properness to F(V)∪K′ for a compact neighborhood V; equivariance gives local finiteness for the pulled-back labels. Closure and continuity give a finite set of relative returns via Γ(K′). For δ<1/4, differing values force one point into K′ and ‖k−h‖≤2δ‖h‖ yields ‖h‖≤2R. For δ≥1/4 use the bound 0≤ψ≤2/m. Composing with normalization and correction gives a relative modulus Cψ C_r C_n(1+H). Moving-frame differentiation and the positive lower bound for H give a constant times H.",
